+# Docker Desktop disk migration recovery and volume inventory
+
+Docker Desktop 4.85 on Windows copied the stopped WSL data disk to the new
+NTFS drive but treated Robocopy exit status 1 as failure and retained the old
+storage setting. The WSL UI then refused the existing destination. Source and
+destination were preserved; no force-kill or WSL shutdown was used.
+
+Upstream reports: <https://github.com/docker/desktop-feedback/issues/550> and
+<https://github.com/docker/desktop-feedback/issues/548>, observed 2026-09-09.
+Microsoft defines code 1 as successful copying:
+<https://learn.microsoft.com/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/robocopy>.
+
+Recovery work adds bounded offline copy, adoption, and service-socket recovery
+commands. Adoption uses the exact `CustomWslDistroDir` key observed in Docker's
+own migration log. The first attempt using the GUI field name was ignored and
+was removed. Settings backups, repeated detached/process checks, source
+retention and explicit post-restart verification are required.
+
+The initial Desktop copy failed containerd's bbolt database integrity check:
+`panic: assertion failed: Page expected to be: 2087, but self identifies as 0`.
+Rollback to the retained original recovered all 13 volumes and eight identical
+model repositories. A fresh copy now requires independent full-file SHA-256
+verification before adoption; matching sizes and VHD identifiers alone were
+insufficient. The fresh 436,154,138,624-byte copy passed SHA-256 verification,
+booted successfully on the new drive, and preserved all thirteen volumes and
+eight repository metadata records exactly. After candidate testing and exact
+incumbent restoration passed direct and authenticated routed checks, both
+detached duplicate VHDX files were removed using exact path whitelists and
+fresh attachment/configuration checks. The verified destination stayed attached
+and Qwen stayed healthy. This returned approximately 406 GiB to the old drive.
+Incumbent smoke, JSON, long-context needle, tools, streaming
+tools and tool-result checks all passed after restart. Cold capacity cells also
+completed successfully on the migrated disk.
+
+Desktop also failed on stale AF_UNIX sockets for inference, secrets-engine,
+vfkit, and OTel. Quarantining only exact zero-byte AF_UNIX sockets after all
+Desktop processes exited restored startup. No credentials were read or changed.
+Related upstream report: <https://github.com/docker/desktop-feedback/issues/460>.
+
+Read-only diagnosis also found Docker Engine's storage report uses `Volumes`,
+while model-cache inventory reads only `LocalVolumes`. The product reports
+zero volumes incorrectly. The compatibility parser now accepts both formats.
+Both format regressions pass. The final inventory retains all original thirteen
+volumes and eight repositories, plus the candidate cache additions; no model
+cache or Docker volume was removed. Final restoration also found no orphaned
+native KV-offload shared-memory files.
